AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00002606 "Sauvignon blanc is a green-skinned grape variety that originates from the Bordeaux region of France. The grape most likely gets its name from the French words sauvage (\"wild\") and blanc (\"white\") due to its early origins as an indigenous grape in South West France."@en)
